==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|hlaibaz|lang=ang}}, from Indo-European ''*kel-, *klei-''.  Cognate with Old High German ''[[hleib]]'' (German ''[[Laib]]''), Old Norse ''[[hleifr]]'' (Old Swedish ''lēver''), Gothic {{l|got|𐌷𐌻𐌰𐌹𐍆𐍃}}.  The Indo-European root is also the source of Ancient Greek {{term|lang=grc|κλίβανος}} ‘baking oven’, Old Slavic ''chlěb’'' (Russian {{l|ru|хлеб}} ‘bread’).

